# hsm-sim 0.1.0: repack
# Ten 100 MB files fill tape T01. Deleting or overwriting a file does not
# erase its tape copy: the space becomes dead until the whole cartridge is
# repacked. When T01 drops below the auto-repack threshold of 50 % live data,
# a scan queues a repack that needs two drives (read T01, write a scratch
# tape) and returns T01 to scratch. Tape T02, whose files are all deleted,
# is reclaimed without mounting anything. An overwrite during migration
# leaves a copy that is stale the moment it lands.
# cache 3000 MB, watermarks 60% high / 20% low
# 2 drive(s), 4 tape(s) x 1000 MB, mount 60 s, seek 20 s, 50 MB/s
# scan every 600 s, migrate after 300 s, auto-repack below 50% live

